  "question": {
    "text": "A compound <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is used in preparation of washing soda to recover ammonia in Solvay's process. When <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> is bubbled through an aqueous solution of <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> , the solution turns milky. It is used in white washing due to disinfectant nature. What is the chemical formula of A?",
